## What shipped

`RegenerateSectionFn` (`services/qms-generation/src/regenerate-section.ts`,
AiStack, DETERMINISTIC name `cumplify-docgen-regen-<env>` — the state
machine's no-cycle pattern) invoked synchronously by QmsFn's
`regenerateSection` case (requestImsExport→ExportFn dispatch pattern, M1-role
gated). Compose runs IN-PROCESS via the ComposeSection handler import — the
one door to Bedrock is unchanged (fn added to the one-door count pin, now 10).

Flow: guards (`RUN_NOT_FOUND` / `RUN_NOT_FINALIZED` / `SECTION_NOT_FOUND`) →
section reset to 'pending' with REVIEW STATE CLEARED (APR-1 is not
inheritable) → standard compose path (GAP-before-model-call, guardedText,
checker+retry, honest failed) → version writeback in ONE txn:
- NEW manual version (MAX+1, `v<n>.json`, assembled from ALL current sections)
- NEW clause-doc version for the section — or the clause document CREATED
  when the section was previously failed and shipped none (regeneration is
  the PARTIAL-run repair path); STILL-failed ships no clause version
- correlation-matrix version when the section kind changed
- master-list version with EVERY entry re-pointed at its latest version —
  closes the Task-9 carry-forward (exports pinned clause docs at v1)
- run status recomputed (failed>0 → partial, else complete)
Audit: `Generation.SectionRegenerated` registered in audit-trail-registry +
contracts/events.md (standing lesson) same commit. Assertion ledger stays
append-only: new sentences append; prior rows remain the v(n-1) history.

